      "side": 1,
      "message": "My thinking is that this change (OverrideInput) inhibits batching for these cases (shader on the paint with non-opaque paint alpha). It also disables coverage-as-alpha. Many of our existing helper FPs had that side effect, including OverrideInput and - by extension - MulChildByInputAlpha.\n\nBut we instead wrapped this with the helper FP I described in the comment above, batching would work (no more uniform color - ops could continue to turn paint color into vertex color). I\u0027m not sure about coverage-as-alpha, though - honestly, after seeing how many shaders were/are *always* returning FPs that don\u0027t allow it (but often accidentally, because of wrapper FPs), I wonder:\n  - How often it triggers?\n  - How often would it be legal, and we\u0027re incorrectly disabling it?\n  - How important is it to preserve it in this code path (shader + paint alpha)?",
